      "claim": "Actions of proving the tenor are appropriate to the court of Session.",
      "tag": "enduring",
      "quote_britannica": "Actions of proving the tenor are, on account of their importance, appropriate to the court of Sellon",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The law of diligence is part of the law of actions in Scots private law."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Summonses replaced brives after the establishment of the College of Justice.",
      "tag": "dropped",
      "quote_britannica": "But fummonies were, immediately upon the infiltration of the college of Jultices, introduced in the place of brives.",
      "quote_wikipedia": null
    },
    {
      "claim": "Defenders within the kingdom are allowed seventy-one days for the first and second diets of appearance.",
      "tag": "dropped",
      "quote_britannica": "I like to within the kingdom, seventy one and life days, for the lift and second diets of appearances, mult be allowed him for that purpose",
      "quote_wikipedia": null
